      "math_academy_id": "q-313855",
      "knowledge_point_id": "660e7de2-aeea-55ad-971b-3c137ccb1521",
      "knowledge_point": "Determining a Rate of Change Given a Related Rate and an Explicit Function",
      "problem": "Given that $y=-{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-5x$ for $x=x(t),$ and that $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=-3$ at the point where $x=2,$ evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}$ at that point.\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-5x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-5x) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-5x) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (-3{x}^{2}+8x-5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=-3$ and $x=2,$ and solve for $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =(-3)\\cdot (-3\\cdot (2)^{2}+8\\cdot (2)-5)=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
